{"ts": "2026-11-02T16:09:00.363613Z", "run_id": "r-20261102T1606Z-fa14", "unit": "openspec:add-web-flow-graph", "seq": 12, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-006", "id": "Q-006", "status": "answered", "reason": "The parity test asserts exactly the scenario (block, human.form, switch, end fixtures, loop over NODE_KINDS, five non-node inputs, GRAPH_NODE_KINDS deep-equals NODE_KINDS). layout.ts and src/authoring/format/nodes.ts have identical switch tables and the two kind lists match entry for entry. Nothing here is observable through a page, so the missing e2e test is not a gap.", "called": true, "tasks": [], "target": "H-62f40190", "kind": "verdict", "batch": "Q-006+5", "batch_size": 5, "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.383976, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "e995be2216df5567b4587c3a052f429527d430e6db0a73a2513d4270e0afbf58", "checked": [{"ref": "test/web-flow-graph/successor-parity.test.ts:51", "quote": "for (const kind of NODE_KINDS) {", "claim": "The Node test compares successorTargets with successorFields for every kind of NODE_KINDS."}, {"ref": "test/web-flow-graph/successor-parity.test.ts:71", "quote": "assert.deepEqual(GRAPH_NODE_KINDS, NODE_KINDS);", "claim": "The test asserts the two kind lists are deep-equal."}, {"ref": "web/src/flow-graph/layout.ts:104", "quote": "case \"human.form\":\n    case \"delegate\":\n      add(\"/next\", node[\"next\"]);\n      add(\"/on_timeout\", node[\"on_timeout\"]);", "claim": "The local successor table gives next then on_timeout for human.form and delegate."}, {"ref": "src/authoring/format/nodes.ts:97", "quote": "case \"human.form\":\n    case \"delegate\":\n      add(\"/next\", node.next);\n      add(\"/on_timeout\", node.on_timeout, false);", "claim": "U22's successorFields gives the same paths in the same order for those kinds."}, {"ref": "src/authoring/format/types.ts:33", "quote": "export const NODE_KINDS: readonly NodeKind[] = [", "claim": "NODE_KINDS lists the same fourteen kinds in the same order as GRAPH_NODE_KINDS in layout.ts."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/web-flow-graph/spec.md#scenario-the-successor-table-agrees-with-the-format-model", "quote": "a test under `test/web-flow-graph/` gives `successorTargets` and U22's `successorFields`", "claim": "The criterion itself places its check in a Node test of internal functions."}]}
